  "nl_text": "The database schema for the database named rschema_0436 consists of 9 tables. The tables are described as follows:\n1. The `administrator` table is used to store information about the administrators of the website. It includes fields such as `administrator_id`, `username`, `password`, `email`, `creation_time`, and `update_time`. The `administrator_id` is the primary key of this table.\n2. The `news_article` table is used to store information about the news articles published on the website. It includes fields such as `article_id`, `article_title`, `article_content`, `article_author`, `publish_time`, `article_category`, `article_tags`, `creation_time`, and `update_time`. The `article_id` is the primary key of this table.\n3. The `website_information` table is used to store information about the website itself. It includes fields such as `website_id`, `website_name`, `website_logo`, `copyright_information`, `creation_time`, and `update_time`. The `website_id` is the primary key of this table.\n4. The `member` table is used to store information about the members of the website. It includes fields such as `member_id`, `username`, `password`, `email`, `registration_time`, and `update_time`. The `member_id` is the primary key of this table.\n5. The `advertisement` table is used to store information about the advertisements posted on the website. It includes fields such as `advertisement_id`, `advertisement_title`, `advertisement_content`, `advertisement_publish_time`, `creation_time`, and `update_time`. The `advertisement_id` is the primary key of this table.\n6. The `message` table is used to store information about the messages posted by members on news articles. It includes fields such as `message_id`, `user_id`, `article_id`, `message_content`, `message_time`, `reply_content`, and `reply_time`. The `message_id` is the primary key of this table and `user_id` and `article_id` are foreign keys referencing the `member` and `news_article` tables respectively.\n7. The `administrator_publish_news` table is used to link the administrators and the news articles they publish. It includes fields such as `administrator_id` and `article_id`. Both are primary keys and foreign keys referencing the `administrator` and `news_article` tables respectively.\n8. The `administrator_manage_advertisement` table is used to link the administrators and the advertisements they manage. It includes fields such as `administrator_id` and `advertisement_id`. Both are primary keys and foreign keys referencing the `administrator` and `advertisement` tables respectively.\n9. The `user_message` table is used to link the members and the messages they post. It includes fields such as `member_id` and `message_id`. Both are primary keys and foreign keys referencing the `member` and `message` tables respectively.\nAll tables have been set up with the InnoDB engine and the default character set is utf8mb3. The tables are designed to maintain data integrity by enforcing primary key and foreign key constraints. The delete and update rules are set to CASCADE, meaning that if a record in the referenced table is deleted or updated, the corresponding records in the referencing table will also be deleted or updated.",
  "gold_question": "Functional description of news management system\n\nAdministrator functions:\n1. News article entry: Administrators can enter new news articles, including title, content, author, release time, etc.\n2. News article management: Administrators can edit, delete, classify, label, and other operations on published news articles.\n3. Website information settings: Administrators can set basic information of the website, such as name, logo, copyright information, etc.\n4. Member information management: Administrators can manage the website's member information, including adding, deleting, modifying, and checking member information.\n5. Advertising management: Administrators can publish, edit, and delete advertisements.\n6. Message management: Administrators can view, reply to, and delete users' messages under news articles.\n\nUser functions:\n1. Registration and login: Users can access the website through the registration and login functions.\n2. News information query: Users can query and view news information on the website.\n3. Post comments: Users can post comments under news articles.\n4. Search function: Users can search for specific news articles through the search function.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0436.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0436\nCREATE TABLE `administrator` (\n  `administrator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`administrator_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `news_article` (\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `article_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `article_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `article_author` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `publish_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `article_category` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `article_tags` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`article_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `website_information` (\n  `website_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `website_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `website_logo` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `copyright_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`website_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `member` (\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`member_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `advertisement` (\n  `advertisement_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `advertisement_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `advertisement_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `advertisement_publish_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`advertisement_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `message` (\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `message_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `message_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `reply_content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reply_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `message_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `message_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`article_id`) REFERENCES `news_article` (`article_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `administrator_publish_news` (\n  `administrator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`administrator_id`, `article_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `administrator_publish_news_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`administrator_id`) REFERENCES `administrator` (`administrator_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `administrator_publish_news_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`article_id`) REFERENCES `news_article` (`article_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `administrator_manage_advertisement` (\n  `administrator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `advertisement_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`administrator_id`, `advertisement_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `administrator_manage_advertisement_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`administrator_id`) REFERENCES `administrator` (`administrator_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `administrator_manage_advertisement_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`advertisement_id`) REFERENCES `advertisement` (`advertisement_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_message` (\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`member_id`, `message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_message_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_message_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`message_id`) REFERENCES `message` (`message_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
